366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Small properties in Rawalpindi experienced a remarkable surge of 207% in 2012, followed by 53% growth in 2013. This was followed by more moderate growth from 2014 to 2019, with fluctuations between 2% and 11% annually. In 2024, a modest 5% growth indicated stable demand. Medium properties in Rawalpindi have followed a gradual and steady growth trajectory, gaining momentum in 2014 with a 74% increase. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consistent growth has been observed in recent years, with a 31% increase in both 2022 and 2023, and 11% growth in 2024, suggesting increasing demand for medium-sized homes. Rawalpindi's large property market experienced extreme volatility from 2012 to 2024. After a modest 10% growth in 2012, it surged dramatically to 111% in 2013, followed by 24% in 2014. The market then cooled, facing slight contraction and stagnation from 2016 to 2018. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A strong recovery began in 2020 with 37% growth, maintaining momentum through 2023. However, 2024 saw a sharp reversal with a 16% decline, highlighting the market's unpredictable nature. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
